.\" zex(1) — Zainium eXecutor & Package Manager
.\" Process with: man ./man/zex.1
.TH ZEX 1 "2026-06-27" "zex 5.0.0" "Zainium OS"
.SH NAME
zex \- Zainium eXecutor & Package Manager
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B elevate zex
.I <command>
.RI [ options ]
.RI [ args ]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B zex
is the native package manager for
.BR ZainiumOS .
It is a BusyBox-style multicall binary: a single ELF that dispatches to
11 sub-commands via
.B argv[0]
symlinks or an explicit command name.
.PP
.B zex
operates across four package tiers:
.TP
.B T1 — Zainium native
Packages in the
.I .zex
format (tar.zst), sourced from
.IR archive.zainiumdynamics.tech .
These are built against musl or relibc with no glibc dependency.
.TP
.B T2 — Alpine Linux
Packages in the
.I .apk
format from Alpine Linux mirrors. Verified via Ed25519 signature.
.TP
.B T3 — Void Linux (musl)
Packages in the
.I .xbps
format from the Void Linux musl repository.
.TP
.B T4 — Chimera Linux
Packages named
.I .apk
but in apk-tools v3's binary "ADB" container format \(em
.B not
the gzip-tar format Alpine uses. Verified via RSA-SHA512 over the ADB
signature block.
.PP
All packages install into the
.I /overlayer/zexlib/union/
userland tree. The immutable core
.RI ( /overlayer/syshub/ )
is updated separately via
.BR "elevate zex syshub" .
.SH COMMANDS
.TP
.B install \fI<pkg>...\fR
Install one or more packages. Dependencies are resolved by a breadth-first
search with tier-affinity preference, real version-constraint checking,
and bidirectional conflict checking; each package is downloaded from the
highest-priority tier that provides it and cryptographically verified
against that tier's real signature scheme, then atomically installed.
Supports
.B \-\-lock\-out
/
.B \-\-from\-lock
/
.B \-\-verify\-lock
for reproducible installs. See
.BR zex-install (1).
.TP
.B remove \fI<pkg>...\fR
Remove installed packages. Reads the receipt file to find every installed
file and removes them exactly. See
.BR zex-remove (1).
.TP
.B update
Fetch latest index from all configured mirrors, diff against installed
packages, and apply all available upgrades to both userland and syshub.
See
.BR zex-update (1).
.TP
.B uland \-\-u
Upgrade userland packages only (T1–T4 tiers).
.TP
.B syshub \-\-u
Upgrade the immutable syshub base. Performs an atomic swap:
build in
.I /overlayer/syshub.new/
then rename to live.
.TP
.B search \fI<query>\fR
Search all four tiers for packages matching the query.
See
.BR zex-search (1).
.TP
.B doctor [\-\-fix]
Audit the system for registry corruption, missing files, broken symlinks,
and glibc contamination. With
.B \-\-fix
attempts automatic repair. See
.BR zex-doctor (1).
.TP
.B rollback \fI<tx-id>\fR
Revert a previous install/upgrade transaction. See
.BR zex-rollback (1).
.TP
.B sweep [\-\-dry\-run] [\-\-aggressive]
Clean package cache, temp files, and orphaned staging directories.
See
.BR zex-sweep (1).
.TP
.B inspect \fI<pkg>\fR
Deep-inspect an installed package: version, files, shared library
dependencies, integrity check. See
.BR zex-inspect (1).
.TP
.B depends \fI<pkg>\fR
Show the dependency tree for a package. See
.BR zex-depends (1).
.TP
.B why \fI<pkg>\fR
Show reverse dependencies — which installed packages depend on
.IR <pkg> .
See
.BR zex-why (1).
.TP
.B pin \fI<pkg>\fR [\-\-reason \fI<text>\fR]
Lock a package at its current version, blocking upgrades.
.TP
.B unpin \fI<pkg>\fR
Release a version lock.
.TP
.B pins
List all currently pinned packages.
.TP
.B history [\-\-package \fI<name>\fR] [\-n \fI<count>\fR]
Show the unified install/upgrade/remove audit trail recorded across all
commands to
.IR /var/lib/zex/history.json .
See
.BR zex-history (1).
.TP
.B \-i \fI<file>\fR [\-\-root \fI<path>\fR]
Install a local
.IR .zex ", " .apk ,
or
.I .xbps
file directly.
By default files are installed into
.IR /overlayer/zexlib/union/ .
.TP
.B \-\-root \fI<path>\fR
.DT
.BR DEV\-ONLY .
Override the install root for local
.B \-i
installs.
Intended for developer testing and CI fixtures only — not for production
system installs.
Production installs must use the default
.I /overlayer/zexlib/union/
path so Quantra's OverlayFS upperdir stays consistent.
.TP
.B \-e \fI<file>\fR [\-o \fI<dir>\fR]
Extract the contents of a package archive to a directory.
.SH FILE SYSTEM LAYOUT
.TP
.I /overlayer/syshub/
Immutable base system. Contains
.IR bin/ ", " lib/ ", " lib64/ ", " include/ ", " share/ ", " etc/ ,
and the GCC 15.3 musl cross-compiler at
.IR x86_64\-zainium\-linux\-musl/ .
.TP
.I /overlayer/zexlib/
Mutable userland area managed by
.BR zex .
.TP
.I /overlayer/zexlib/union/
Union mount root. Userland packages install
.IR bin/ ", " lib/ ", " share/ ,
etc. here.
.TP
.I /overlayer/zexlib/registry/installed/
One
.I <name>.toml
receipt file per installed package.
.TP
.I /overlayer/zexlib/registry/packages.toml
Installed package index.
.TP
.I /overlayer/zexlib/registry/pinned.toml
Pinned package list.
.TP
.I /overlayer/zexlib/transactions/
Transaction snapshots for rollback.
.TP
.I /overlayer/zexlib/registry/cache/
Downloaded package cache, split by tier.
.TP
.I /overlayer/zexlib/tmp/
Temporary staging area for downloads and extraction.
.TP
.I /overlayer/syshub/engine/services/zex_services.toml
Mirror configuration.
.TP
.I /overlayer/syshub/engine/services/syshub.toml
Immutable base package manifest.
.SH SECURITY
.B zex
verifies every package against its tier's real upstream signature scheme:
.B Ed25519
+
.B Blake3
for native
.I .zex
(T1), RSA-PKCS1v15 over the compressed control tarball for Alpine
.I .apk
(T2), RSA-SHA256 over the whole file with TOFU key pinning for Void
.I .xbps
(T3), and RSA-SHA512 over the ADB signature block for Chimera
.I .apk
(T4).
.PP
All operations that modify
.I /overlayer/syshub/
or install packages require root privileges via
.BR elevate (1).
.PP
Sandbox isolation is applied during post-install scripts via the
.BR elevate (1)
privilege layer.
.SH EXAMPLES
Install
.B ripgrep:
.PP
.nf
    elevate zex install ripgrep
.fi
.PP
Install from a local file:
.PP
.nf
    elevate zex -i /path/to/myapp-1.0.zex
.fi
.PP
Search for a package:
.PP
.nf
    zex search "fuzzy finder"
.fi
.PP
Pin
.B gcc
to prevent accidental upgrade:
.PP
.nf
    elevate zex pin gcc --reason "kernel ABI stability"
.fi
.PP
Full system update:
.PP
.nf
    elevate zex update
.fi
.PP
Doctor with auto-fix:
.PP
.nf
    elevate zex doctor --fix
.fi
