.SH ZEX FMT — PACKAGE AUTHORING
.B "zex fmt"
is the secure package builder integrated into the
.B zex
multicall binary. It packs, signs, and verifies
.I .zex
packages.
.TP
.B "zex fmt pack" \fI<dir>\fR \fB\-\-version\fR \fI<v>\fR
Build a signed
.I .zex
package from a source directory. Runs:
.RS
.TP 3
1. Layout policy enforcement (no /usr/ references)
.TP 3
2. Secrets scan (no hardcoded credentials)
.TP 3
3. Rust security audit (cargo audit, clippy, unsafe count)
.TP 3
4. C/C++ static analysis (if applicable)
.TP 3
5. Permission audit (no setuid/setgid files)
.TP 3
6. Blake3 + SHA-512 hashing, Ed25519 signing
.TP 3
7. Produce
.I <name>_<version>.zex
and install receipt
.RE
.TP
.B "zex fmt unpack" \fI<file>\fR [\fB\-o\fR \fI<dir>\fR]
Extract and verify a
.I .zex
package.
.TP
.B "zex fmt verify" \fI<file>\fR
Verify signature and integrity only (no extraction).
.TP
.B "zex fmt inspect" \fI<file>\fR
Show embedded security report and manifest metadata.
.TP
.B "zex fmt review" \fI<file.locked>\fR \fB\-\-slot\fR \fI<1\-5>\fR \fB\-\-reviewer\fR \fI<id>\fR \fB\-\-status\fR \fI<approved|rejected>\fR
Fill a maintainer review slot in a
.I .zex.locked
artifact.
.TP
.B "zex fmt keygen" [\fB\-o\fR \fI<output-dir>\fR] [\fB\-\-force\fR]
Generate a real Ed25519 signing keypair for use by
.BR "zex fmt pack" .
Writes
.I signing.key
(hex, private, mode 0600) and
.I trust.pub
(base64, public) into
.I <output-dir>
(default: current directory).
.B \-\-force
overwrites existing key files. Without a real keypair on the builder
machine,
.B "zex fmt pack"
silently falls back to a hardcoded, publicly-known dev key — fine for
local testing, never for a real release. See
.BR ZEX-FORMAT.md
for full key-placement instructions.
